# ==========================================================================
# CNSPK · Cloudflare Pages redirects  (task 16.1 · Requirements 1.3, 1.4)
# ==========================================================================
# One mechanism owns each redirect. No double hops.
#
#   www -> apex (308, path preserved) ....... Cloudflare Redirect Rule (edge)
#                                             mirrored below for the record
#   HTTP -> HTTPS ........................... Cloudflare "Always Use HTTPS"
#                                             (SSL/TLS > Edge Certificates)
#                                             NOT this file, by design
#   unknown route ........................... /404.html (served automatically
#                                             by Cloudflare Pages; no rule here)
#
# WHY THE www RULE LIVES AT THE EDGE, NOT HERE:
# Cloudflare Pages' `_redirects` matches on path only — its own documentation
# lists domain-level redirects as unsupported, and both hostnames map to the same
# Pages project. So the authoritative implementation is a free Cloudflare
# Redirect Rule (the exact rule is in DEPLOY.md), which fires at the edge before
# the Pages project is reached. The declaration below is kept as a self-describing
# mirror of that intent: if Pages ever honors a host-qualified source, it produces
# the identical single 308 hop, so the two can never disagree or chain.
#
# DNS PREREQUISITE (verified 2025): `www.cloudnativesecurity.pk` currently does
# not resolve at all — NXDOMAIN. Until a DNS record for `www` exists (CNAME to
# the Pages project, proxied), this rule can never fire, because no request ever
# reaches Cloudflare for that hostname. Adding the record is a cutover step in
# DEPLOY.md.
#
# Also note: `_redirects` rules are not applied to requests served by Pages
# Functions, so nothing here affects /api/*.
#
# No legacy path moves are declared: every route in the page map keeps its
# existing path (Requirement 1.6), and /legacy/ stays reachable but is
# disallowed in robots.txt rather than redirected.
# ==========================================================================

# source                                    destination                              code
https://www.cloudnativesecurity.pk/*        https://cloudnativesecurity.pk/:splat    308
